# Radar relevance profile: how to rank items for {{NAME}}

The cloud task reads this every run before writing items. Every item gets `prio`: 1 = priority, 2 = normal (default), 3 = FYI (low).
- prio 3 items still appear (so you know they exist), but in a compact "FYI" strip at the bottom: no checkbox, not in "Coming up", not in counters. Never put a prio-3 item in section action.
- prio 1 = a real deadline you own, something addressed to you, or a strong fit for one of your focus areas. Use sparingly (a handful per day).

This file is written in plain English on purpose: to change how the Radar ranks things, tell your Claude in the gsb-radar folder what you want (e.g. "religious events are FYI for me", "anything about the VC Club is priority") and it edits this file. The next WhatsApp export ships the change.

