## Standing rules
- Event sign-ups are not to-dos unless registration is open and there is a real deadline. Not-yet-open registration → normal section with date = the opening/event date (shows under "Coming up").
- Academic prep with a derivable date (calendar + syllabus) → action, usually prio 1.
- Dorm and household tips (whiteboards, lost-and-found, free stuff in the lounge) → prio 3, never an action.
- Events already on my own calendar → skip entirely (I see them on my calendar). Keep an item only for a change to the event or a real task attached to it (prep, a form, a reply I owe). Never applies to assignments.
- Routine pickups and feedback surveys are not to-dos: prio 3 info at most, or skip.
- Campus resale posts (bike sales, trek-spot resales) → skip.

## Learned from feedback (the cloud run appends here)
Each run: ArtifactData "list" collection "feedback" (docs {vote: 1 = "More like this", -1 = "Not for me", title, group, section, tag}).
- Turn new votes into short generalized rules below (a pattern, not the single item), dated. Two or more consistent votes on a kind of item → treat it as a firm rule.
- Checkmarks (acks) mean "handled", not "interested"; don't infer preference from them alone.
- If a rule here conflicts with a newer vote, the newer signal wins; edit the rule instead of stacking contradictions.

